.th TMAC.NAME VII 5/31/77
.sh NAME
tmac.name \*- standard nroff and troff macro packages
.sh DESCRIPTION
.tr ~
A number of standard macro packages have been written for
use with the UNIX text formatters,
.it nroff(I)
and
.it troff(I).
When using either of these commands,
an argument of the form \fB\*-m\fIname\fR requests inclusion of the file named
\fB/usr/lib/tmac.\fIname\fR.
.s1
The following macro packages are supported by
PWB/UNIX.
All but the last can be used with either
.it nroff
or
.it troff.
The last one works with
.it troff
only.
.if n .ta 7 
.if t .ta .5i 
.de LI
.br
.if t .sp .5v
.if n .ne 5
.if t .ne .6i
.if n .ti 5
.if t .ti \\n(}Iu
\\$1\t\c
..
.s2
.it "Name	Description/Documentation"
.br
.if n .in+7
.if t .in +.5i
.LI a
Same as /usr/man/man0/caa.
See
.it "PWB/UNIX Manual Page Macros"
by E.~M.~Piskorik.
.LI m
PWB/MM;
a unified, general-purpose set of macros for memoranda,
manuals, letters, etc.
See
.it "PWB/MM \- Programmer's Workbench Memorandum Macros"
by D.~W.~Smith and J.~R.~Mashey.
.LI org
BTL organization chart macros.
.LI uom
UNIX Operations Manual macros;
uses \-mm.
.LI v
View graph and slide macros.
See
.it "PWB/UNIX View Graph and Slide Macros"
by T.~A.~Dolotta and D.~W.~Smith.
.i0
.sh "SEE ALSO"
nroff(I), troff(I)
.tr ~~
